Juno Metrics Plan: Possible Duplicate Suggestions
Illustrative assumptions for the theoretical product.
1. What should change: Juno should help PMs identify ideas that may express the same customer need, verify the source evidence, and decide whether to link them without losing distinct requests or support.
2. Goal metric: Percentage of duplicate suggestions that PMs thumbs-up. Estimated baseline without Juno: 80% of manually surfaced potential matches get a thumbs-up. Target with Juno: at least 95%.
3. Usage metric: Number of Juno suggestions PMs review each week. Pattern to watch: PMs keep using it week after week; declining use may signal low trust.
4. Review date: December 17, 2026, after a four-week pilot.
5. Stop condition: Stop using Juno if fewer than 80% of its suggestions get a thumbs-up for two consecutive weeks.
